etely destroyed  by the saiyans under frieza's orders he  wants revenge against frieza but he  doesn't have the power  so he wishes to be the greatest warrior  in the universe notably  the dragon mentions that this wouldn't  count the gods themselves  this is one of those wishes that i  wasn't really sure if it would be  possible to realize or not  not everything is fair game for a wish  from a dragon since the power of the  dragons  is limited i assume this wouldn't be  possible however in this case  it would be possible if as we find out  later  he shortened his lifespan from 150 years  left to  three years left as the dragon explains  he is able to multiply granola's current  strength by condensing  any and all power he could have  accumulated in his lifetime and the dude  agrees  saying he will do whatever it takes to  get revenge  at first i wasn't a big fan of this dude  because he wasn't one of our main  lovable characters and i felt like when  he was on screen it was taking away from  the time those guys would have  and he also didn't seem strong enough to  even be relevant  but he's grown on me and he's definitely  strong enough now i'm a sucker for good  revenge stories and granola's definitely  got that going for him and i really like  how much this arc is incorporating  history by involving the history of  frieza and the saiyans that we're  already well aware of  we also jump back to vegeta training  with beerus  to use the god of destruction powers  while goku  is refining ultra instinct i gotta admit  i wasn't sure  how it was going to go when vegeta said  he would find his own path to surpass  goku but i like this approach god of  destruction vegeta  is hella hype and i'm just glad that  vegeta is going to be able to stay close  to goku's level  and rival it somehow watching a god of  destruction vegeta versus mastered ultra  instinct goku face off down the line  would be  so awesome as beerus is teaching vegeta  about the destruction move he explains  that the target is completely erased  from  existence they turn something into  nothing and when matter is destroyed  it releases a heap of energy beerus says  the explosion is the highlight of using  destruction i also love the fact that as  he's training vegeta he's reading comics  just like elder kai and dragon ball z  when he was training gohan good to see  that the gods respect  manga if even the gods read them then  you can bet it's a good use of our time  as goku is wondering if beerus is really  training vegeta  whis asks him if that's a problem and he  responds and i quote navaji is his own  man  i'm here to polish ultra instinct and  quote  and he just sits there meditating again  i love this i love how they each have  their different  paths and that there's clearly more than  one way to get to the final destination  which is to be the strongest in the  universe philosophically i prefer  goku's path but you can't deny that god  of destruction vegeta is such a cool  idea it's like major vegeta on steroids  and we all know how cool  that was even if that wasn't the most  moral version of him  and i love how as these two are  competing among each other to become the  strongest we says  yeah but the strongest may turn out to  be someone else entirely  obviously we know this is gonna be  granola at this point but i like how no  matter how strong our fighters get  there's always the chance of someone  else entering the picture and  challenging them if you're number one  today and you stop training and putting  in the work that doesn't mean you'll be  number one tomorrow you gotta keep  working on it and it's never guaranteed  and  it's a never-ending journey and  adventure it's also funny how the oracle  fish  says the strongest war in the universe  will rise soon and of course vegeta  thinks it will be him after he masters  destruction and that would have been a  good guess  if it wasn't for granola nevertheless we  get a very hyped moment for vegeta and  vegeta fans  should be loving the story right now  vegeta actually succeeds  in causing the explosion that results  from destruction  sure he starts off with the tiniest  pebble but it means he can do it  and as he implies he'll soon be  destroying larger and larger things  as he gains more and more mastery god of  destruction vegeta seems pretty  inevitable now  even if he doesn't actually take on the  specific role as a god of destruction  i still feel like that's going to be the  best thing to call him but we'll see if  they give us  any other names for it in the manga and  although i love the power upgrade i  would never actually want vegeta to  become a god of destruction in the sense  that he has to work as beerus does  because i much prefer him having  adventures on earth and chilling with  bulma and trunks when he gets a chance  i absolutely love to see how genuinely  delighted goku is for vegeta's  accomplishment  you know if the roles were reversed  vegeta would probably be mad and envious  that goku accomplished something he  didn't  in these moments goku is like the  perfect role model for how we should  behave in life and at other times when  he spares enemies who could destroy his  family and the universe he's not so  perfect which is okay too  we then jump to the planet cereal and  you gotta love granola super saiyan 3  like hair  right now very cool they do a good job  of actually  translating his newfound power and  confidence through his expression and  aura  he's definitely got a different vibe  about him now just as vegeta destroyed a  small pebble  here granola similarly destroys a large  boulder granola doesn't know what  technique that  was but clearly the story is suggesting  that it's the power of destruction  not only that he's got a better grasp of  it than vegeta from the looks of it but  this is just what it looks like right  now we're sure to find out more about it  in the future we then get an  interesting discussion between granola  and 